.TH XD\-SYSDM 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-sysdm \- System Properties and Device Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-sysdm
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SY xd\-sysdm
.B \-\-devmgr
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-sysdm
is Windows 2000's System Properties (Control Panel > System) with Linux
inside:
.TP
.B General
The distribution, kernel, owner, CPU, firmware and memory.
.TP
.B Network Identification
The computer's name and description, through systemd-hostnamed.
.TP
.B Hardware
Device Manager, built from udev, with each device's driver and details;
the loaded kernel modules; Secure Boot and module signing; power profiles.
.TP
.B User Profiles
Home folders and their sizes.
.TP
.B Advanced
Swap and zram; the user's environment variables; the boot loader's
entries and crash handling.
.PP
System changes go through the system services and their polkit checks, so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for a password when one is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n :
0 General, 1 Network Identification, 2 Hardware, 3 User Profiles,
4 Advanced.
.TP
.B \-\-devmgr
Device Manager on its own.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/environment.d/99\-xeondesktop.conf
The environment variables set on the Advanced tab, which
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1)
and systemd's user manager read at the next logon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-control (1),
.BR hostnamectl (1),
.BR environment.d (5)
